    "body": "The output is time since epoch in millis as an integer, the same as `starship time`. This should be a drop-in replacement. Am I missing something? I used this approach because `show_milliseconds` is an option we support for `cmd_duration`. If not, there are simpler and more-widely supported options like `$SECONDS`.\r\n\r\nSample Output:\r\n```\r\n~ ❯ starship time\r\n1602149653499\r\n~ ❯ ((currentTimeInEpoch = int(rint($EPOCHREALTIME * 1000)))) && echo $currentTimeInEpoch\r\n1602149677644\r\n```",
    "created_at": "2020-10-08T09:36:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-06T19:04:13Z",
